Orchestrator: SDD

Purpose:
  Autonomous Project Orchestrator. Unifies all engines into a single
  agent lifecycle. Handles greenfield and brownfield modes. Transforms
  user intent into architecture, tasks, workflow, implementation, and release.

Owns: ./

Modes:
  AUTO — AI decides low-risk items
  SUPERVISED — AI recommends, human approves major decisions
  STRICT — Human approval required for architecture, security, DB migration, release
  AUDIT — Analysis only, no modifications
  READ_ONLY — Project analysis, no code changes

Rules:
  [OD1] Default mode is AUTO for standard projects.
  [OD2] STRICT mode requires human approval for critical decisions.
  [OD3] READ_ONLY mode never modifies source code.
  [OD4] AI MUST stop on critical ambiguity.
  [OD5] AI MUST request human approval for HIGH/CRITICAL risk decisions.
  [OD6] AI MUST NOT restart workflow on resume.
  [OD7] Agent state MUST be persisted after each step.
  [OD8] Crash recovery MUST resume from exact state, not restart.
  [OD9] All user input MUST be normalized to structured intent.
  [OD10] Intent MUST include risk assessment.
  [OD11] Pipeline is adaptive, not linear.
  [OD12] Existing project starts with discovery, not architecture.
  [OD13] Multi-agent execution requires Role, Scope, Context, Permission, Task, Communication, Ownership.
  [OD14] Every agent MUST have exactly one primary role.
  [OD15] Agent responsibility is explicit, not implicit.
  [OD16] Every task has exactly one owner.
  [OD17] Handoff transfers context package, not full context.
  [OD18] Orchestrator is NOT necessarily an LLM agent — workflow is deterministic.
  [OD19] Agents do NOT negotiate directly — all communication goes through orchestrator.
  [OD20] Parallel agents MUST have synchronization points.
  [OD21] Agent isolation prevents partial work interference.
  [OD22] Reviewer is independent from coder — confirmation bias prevention.
  [OD23] Critical tasks require two-agent verification.
  [OD24] Security veto cannot be overridden by majority vote.
  [OD25] Agents have autonomy but NOT authority.
  [OD26] Authority comes from SDD governance, not agent self-declaration.
  [OD27] Partial progress does not automatically mean workflow FAILED.
  [OD28] Agent memory MUST be controlled, versioned, audited.
  [OD29] Agent quotas prevent runaway agents.
  [OD30] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to any output.
  [OD31] Agent MUST NOT use emojis or decorative symbols in headers or titles.

Intent:
  Types: BUG | FEATURE | REFACTOR | SECURITY | PERFORMANCE | DEPLOY | ANALYZE | PLAN
  Structure: Intent, Domain, Risk, Constraints, RequiredSkills, LikelySkills
  Rules:
    - All user input MUST be normalized
    - Critical ambiguity MUST trigger clarification
    - Non-critical ambiguity resolved by agent research

State:
  States: DISCOVERING, ANALYZING, PLANNING, WAITING, IMPLEMENTING,
          TESTING, VERIFYING, RELEASING, DEPLOYING, OBSERVING,
          COMPLETED, FAILED
  Persistence: runtime/state.sdd
  Recovery: resume from exact state, no restart

Pipeline:
  New: Intent → Discovery → Analysis → Architecture → Skills →
       Decision → Tasks → Dependencies → Workflow → BDD →
       Implementation → Test → Security → Performance →
       Infrastructure → Release → Deploy → Observe → Learn
  Existing: Intent → Scan → Analysis → Detection → Mapping →
            Conflict → Baseline → Gaps → Tasks → Workflow →
            Parallel Execution
  Rules:
    - Pipeline is adaptive, not linear
    - Cross-layer changes trigger multi-layer task creation
    - Pipeline MUST support pause/resume for human approval

Degradation:
  FULL: all features operational
  REDUCED: skip optional stages, core skills only
  MINIMAL: basic chain only, human approval for all gates
  READ_ONLY: analysis only, no modifications
  Triggers: resource pressure, component failure, repeated failures

ReadOrder:
   1  @modes.sdd
   2  @pipeline.sdd
   3  @routing.sdd

Navigation:
  Orchestrator: @orchestrator/INDEX.sdd
  Modes: @orchestrator/modes.sdd
  Pipeline: @orchestrator/pipeline.sdd
  Routing: @orchestrator/routing.sdd
  Runtime: @runtime/INDEX.sdd
  Context: @context/INDEX.sdd
  Skills: @skills/INDEX.sdd
  Protocol: @protocol/INDEX.sdd
  Graph: @graph/INDEX.sdd
  Tasks: @tasks/INDEX.sdd
  Workflow: @workflow/INDEX.sdd
  Observability: @observability/INDEX.sdd

State: +